# CODEOWNERS — review gate for protected and high-blast-radius paths
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# Work on this repo is increasingly done by AI agents (Claude, Codex,
# Antigravity) opening PRs from `claude/`, `codex/`, and `antigravity/`
# branches. Agents are good at scoped, well-specified changes and bad at
# knowing which changes are irreversible. This file makes the owner a
# required reviewer on the paths where a mistake is expensive, slow to
# detect, or impossible to undo.
#
# The protected domains below come from `AGENTS.md` and
# `.claude/skills/vsa-change-control/`. That skill is authoritative; this
# file is the mechanical enforcement of a subset of it. If the two ever
# disagree, AGENTS.md wins and this file is wrong.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS only *requests* review by default. It becomes a real
# gate when branch protection on `main` enables "Require review from Code
# Owners". As of the last check, `main` had no branch protection at all
# (AGENTS.md L258) — verify with:
#   gh api repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/branches/main/protection
# A 404 means this file is advisory only.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — everything else needs no specific owner
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# (intentionally no global rule; unowned paths stay reviewable by anyone)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database, RLS, and privileged server code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Migrations define the real security boundary. RLS is what actually
# protects member data — the client-side admin check is convenience only.
